{
 "scope": "Fill calibration: how often do wrong word fills of the constraint sheet pass the no-lift key-free\nchecks on the real eyes? (notes/plaintext/fill-calibration.md). Exploratory: a measurement, no decision rule.\n\nA fill gives every body cell a letter while obeying the sheet (default tiers): cells tied by the sheet\nget the same letter. Fresh text comes from a word source (tier x language), written message by message.\nLevels of how much is filled:\n  shared   only cells tied to another cell (the skeleton); every free cell unknown\n  fields   shared + the field slots (resync-window unequal cells, E2 25-34, W4 21-35)\n  free+k   shared + fields + the first k free cells of each message\n  full     every cell\nChecks (key-free, no lifts; guess-check-math.md R1 signature consistency + R2 matching), with '?'\ncells skipped (a window counts only if its endpoints and, for class groupings, its middle are known):\n  gak      every letter its own class\n  vc       digits | vowels | consonants (space with consonants)\n  lds      digits | letters | space\nNumbers: with --digits the field slots hold random digits instead of words.\nPlus the sheet's own rules on visible cells: must-differ pairs differ; for class groupings, the resync\nsame-class pairs share a class.\nControl: true text on synthetic eyes (same fill, encrypted with a random no-lift key for the grouping)\nmust give 0 conflicts at every level.",
